<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian sugar crush - week to July 12.</title>
<headline>Australian sugar crush - week to July 12.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's sugar cane crush totalled 1,507,228 tonnes in the week ended July 12, bringing the crush so far this season to 5.56 million tonnes, cane farmer organisation CANEGROWERS said.</p>
<p>The cumulative crush was equal to the 5.56 million tonnes crushed to the same time last year. CANEGROWERS reported for crushing week five of the 1997 season that average commercial cane sugar (ccs) content was 12.59 percent.</p>
<p>The figures do not include cane crushed in the Ord River region of Western Australia.  </p>
<p>Australian sugar cane crush by region for the week ended July 12 as reported by CANEGROWERS, in tonnes.</p>
<p>CCS = Commercial Cane Sugar (sugar content percent)-</p>
<p>			Crushed   Crushed    CCS	 CCS</p>
<p>			This wk   to Date  this wk   to date</p>
<p> North Qld	 506,709  1,373,143   11.98     11.79</p>
<p> Burdekin	  274,138  1,472,577   13.88     13.37</p>
<p> Central Qld     482,754  1,877,683   12.84     12.54</p>
<p> South Qld	 156,262    462,910   12.85     12.58</p>
<p> Queensland    1,419,863  5,186,313   12.74     12.58</p>
<p> N.South Wales    87,365    376,560   10.24     10.17</p>
<p> Australia     1,507,228  5,562,873   12.59     12.42</p>
<p>				   YEAR AGO</p>
<p> Queensland    1,497,147   5,459,651   12.55     12.15</p>
<p> Australia     1,486,244   5,564,502   12.43     12.12</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Summary - Total cane crushed 39.604 million tonnes (Qld 37.217 million, NSW 2.387 million), sugar produced 5.442 million tonnes 94 n.t., (Qld 5.156 million, NSW 285,616), sugar content (CCS) 13.50 percent (Qld 13.62 percent, NSW 11.63 percent).</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
